# A Pi's first start is a first boot to systemd (/etc/machine-id is
# "uninitialized" in the image), and at a first boot systemd enables every unit
# a preset says to. The image enables what Nova runs itself
# (tools/build-pi-image), so no preset enables anything: systemd's own list
# would add systemd-networkd beside NetworkManager, and homed, sysext and the
# systemd-boot updater, none of which a Pi has a use for. This comes before
# systemd's 90-systemd.preset, and the first line that names a unit decides.
disable *
